Subject: [PATCH 05/42] Add Gate 2 driver script; fix break-glass wording
 precision
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- scripts/run-neura-session.ts: launches a real Prime Agent session in
  NEURA mode through the actual public createAgentSession entry point
  (baseToolsOverride, initialActiveToolNames: ["neurabash"],
  includeGoals: false). Not a permanent CLI flag — baseToolsOverride
  takes real AgentTool instances, and Prime's args parser has no
  pattern for passing objects through string flags; threading a
  research-only mode through the whole CLI pipeline would be
  infrastructure built ahead of evidence. This is the small driver
  the chassis plan's Gate 2 section names as the actual prerequisite.
  Fails loudly if NEURABASH_BIN is unset, per the same section's
  warning that a silent fail-closed would pass Gate 2's letter while
  NeuraBash never ran.

- neurabash-preferred.ts: the original "prefer neurabash" note didn't
  distinguish "avoid ipython for computation" from "ipython remains
  the only path to sub-agent spawning, diffs, attachments, compaction,
  and self-refinement today, use it normally for those." A "break
  glass" framing without that distinction risks the model avoiding
  ipython for tasks that genuinely need it, which would be a real
  functional regression dressed up as a clean experimental result.

